body:
codex-storymodel-collab — CURRENT STATUS, re-derived from main and the tracker.

Short version: the scientific architecture is substantially designed; event segmentation and topic modeling are not implemented as working end-to-end capabilities.

EVENT SEGMENTATION

What exists now:
- provider-neutral BoundaryEvidence with separate semantic, proposition, entity, location, context, world-time, goal, sensory, affect, discourse-cue, and model-vote signals;
- explicit missing/observed estimates and per-signal feature-space provenance;
- FeatureUseLedger as the only route to a BoundaryScore, so circular feature reuse can be audited;
- retained BoundaryBelief values plus a selected NarrativeHierarchy, so losing boundaries need not disappear;
- codecs for those current values.

What is decided:
- two estimands, never collapsed: (A) a task/instruction-conditioned perceptual boundary track and (B) a resolved evidence-backed narrative hierarchy;
- the resolved hierarchy cannot be recycled as human-consensus gold;
- repeated LLM calls are clustered provider/config evidence, not synthetic independent raters, and raw vote fractions are not probabilities;
- no new segment module yet; ownership remains features + acquire + story until a second consumer proves a stable abstraction.

What is not done:
- no unattended proposer/resolver pipeline has been implemented or calibrated;
- current public values still use bare Int for both perceptual grain and structural hierarchy depth, including Map[Int, weights]. That is an active scientific conflation;
- ADR 0004 exists on main but is still Draft. It rules two non-interchangeable coordinates and atomic migration, but its grain vocabulary is unresolved;
- no implementation bead is open for the atomic migration or the multi-provider decision spike.

The real first gate is evidence, not code. The adjudication protocol is decided, and a 17-story/three-family candidate manifest exists, but it is explicitly not frozen: PD/edition sign-offs are blank, no story text has been fetched, and no adjudicated per-rater boundary corpus exists. WOG and the synthetic Anna fixture are regression/diagnostic material, not human-consensus calibration evidence.

TOPIC MODELING

There is no topic-model provider, TopicBasis, TopicMixture, or core Topic identity in current source.

The present design deliberately separates:
1. local topical/cohesion change as one receipted boundary feature (possible today through a namespaced BoundarySignal.Custom);
2. named theme/motif interpretations as evidence-backed DescriptorClaims;
3. corpus-level topic mixtures as a future optional sidecar with a content-addressed basis, only after a concrete cross-corpus analysis requires stable comparable topics.

So topic information has an honest place to enter, but a topic model itself has not been built, admitted, benchmarked, or wired into selection.

RECOMMENDED NEXT DECISION

Ratify ADR 0004 with a protocol-scoped open task-grain identity: exact instruction/version/checksum + judgment domain + grain label, with ordering only inside one declared protocol. Then name a small lawful multi-story diagnostic fixture and the exact acceptance matrix before opening the atomic migration and proposer/resolver spike. The full human-consensus calibration claim must wait for the signed, fetched, adjudicated frozen set; a synthetic diagnostic spike may not be promoted to that claim.

This status is current as of main 95bba070a5849c0381ec5d7c379a66587266ce30 and today's Mote state. I made no repository or tracker mutation beyond this status post.
